    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with a lineup optimized for volume and high-ceiling matchups against vulnerable arms. **Pete Crow-Armstrong** headlines our starters with an elite 72.40 score; his lead-off spot against Wilber Dotel, combined with a significant 14% platoon advantage, positions him as our primary engine for Runs and the scarcest category, SB. Similarly, **Christian Encarnacion-Strand** provides a robust 64.44 rating against Max Scherzer; despite facing a veteran arm, the matchup against a high-ERA starter (5.10 xERA) and the favorable stolen base environment created by Scherzer\u2019s delivery cadence make him a mandatory start in the UTIL spot. **Caleb Durbin** also remains a cornerstone of this squad, buoyed by a 63.75 score and his elite capacity to convert base runners into points, even in a neutral platoon spot against Seth Lugo.\n\nOur most difficult roster decision involved **Lars Nootbaar**, who fell just short of the starting threshold with a 45.24 score. While he remains a steady asset, his projected #9 spot in the batting order\u2014resulting in an 8% negative adjustment\u2014tipped the scales toward the higher-leverage opportunities afforded to **Christian Yelich** and **Josh Smith**. We are keeping a close eye on the official lineups, as the \"Lineup Pending\" status introduces variability across the board. While **Trea Turner** faces a daunting matchup against the elite Chris Sale (2.81 xERA), his raw skill set keeps him in the lineup, though his 53.65 score serves as a reminder that we are prioritizing defensive efficiency against high-tier pitching to preserve our season game caps. We are proceeding with this configuration, keeping **Dillon Dingler** and **Chase Meidroth** on standby should any last-minute defensive shifts or health updates emerge.",
